  "content": {
    "id": "p45-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "In the diagram, the points $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ are on the circumference of a circle, whose centre $O$ lies on $BD$. The chord $AC$ intersects the diameter $BD$ at $Y$. The tangent at $D$ passes through the point $X$. It is given that $\\angle CYB = 100^\\circ$ and $\\angle DCY = 30^\\circ$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p45-q5-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 45 p45-q5-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,line cap=round,line join=round]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\usetikzlibrary{calc,angles,quotes}\n\\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\n\\coordinate (A) at (0:3);\n\\coordinate (B) at (120:3);\n\\coordinate (C) at (260:3);\n\\coordinate (D) at (300:3);\n\\coordinate (Y) at (intersection of A--C and B--D);\n\\coordinate (X) at ($(D)+(30:3.2)$);\n\\coordinate (TL) at ($(D)+(210:2.5)$);\n\\coordinate (TR) at ($(D)+(30:3.8)$);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (O) circle[radius=3];\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (B)--(D) (C)--(A) (B)--(C) (B)--(A) (A)--(D) (C)--(D) (TL)--(TR);\n\\fill[black] (O) circle[radius=1.2pt] (X) circle[radius=1.2pt];\n\\node[above right] at (A) {$A$};\n\\node[above] at (B) {$B$};\n\\node[below left] at (C) {$C$};\n\\node[below] at (D) {$D$};\n\\node[above right] at (O) {$O$};\n\\node[right] at (Y) {$Y$};\n\\node[below] at (X) {$X$};\n\\pic[draw=black,line width=0.4pt,angle radius=8mm,angle eccentricity=1.35,\"$100^\\circ$\"] {angle=C--Y--B};\n\\pic[draw=black,line width=0.4pt,angle radius=9mm,angle eccentricity=1.35,\"$30^\\circ$\"] {angle=D--C--Y};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 76,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 45,
          "sourceRegion": "Question 5, lower-left shared diagram",
          "description": "Unshaded circle with diameter BD, intersecting chord AC, chords BC, BA, AD and CD, and the tangent through D extending on both sides. One figure supports parts a–c. Ordinary geometry and labels are black.",
          "mathematics": "A, B, C and D lie on the circle. B, O, Y and D are collinear in that order; C, Y and A are collinear. The tangent DX is perpendicular to OD. Circle coordinates derive the given angles CYB = 100 degrees and DCY = 30 degrees; the coordinates are construction data, not additional printed givens.",
          "answerVisibility": "Only supplied givens appear; no answer angles or solution annotations."
        },
        "derived": false,
